{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"9fe32aedc6d77f66","name":"card_event_agency_africa","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/events/card_event_agency_africa","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"AGENCY AFRICA","text":"Add to hand a copy of a random known card in the enemy hand.","flavorText":"Agency Africa was a Polish intelligence network in North Africa, run by a Polish Army Officer called Mieczysław Zygfryd Słowikowski codenamed “Rygor”. The agency was run under the cover of an oats factory and a sales and marketing chain which gave him and his agents permits to travel freely in Algeria, Morocco and France. This also gave them access to Axis military units, airports, naval bases and ports where they offered their commodities for sale. Not only was his business a commercial success, but it also gave “Rygor” and his agents access to vital information which they shared with the UK and US intelligence services. The information gathered by Agency Africa was used by the Allies to plan and execute Operation Torch, the successful amphibious landings in North Africa.","faction":"Poland","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_agency_africa","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_agency_africa_title","SourceString":"AGENCY AFRICA","LocalizedString":"AGENCY AFRICA"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_agency_africa_text","SourceString":"Add to hand a copy of a random known card in the enemy hand.","LocalizedString":"Add to hand a copy of a random known card in the enemy hand."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_agency_africa_history","SourceString":"Agency Africa was a Polish intelligence network in North Africa, run by a Polish Army Officer called Mieczysław Zygfryd Słowikowski codenamed “Rygor”. The agency was run under the cove